An error factory is used everywhere, so every stack trace starts inside it. What does adding `Error.captureStackTrace(e, httpError)` change?

```js
function httpError(status, msg) {
  const e = new Error(msg);
  e.status = status;
  Error.captureStackTrace(e, httpError);
  return e;
}
```

What happens when this runs on Node 24?

```js
const assert = require('node:assert');
assert.throws(() => { throw new TypeError('x'); }, RangeError);
```

What does this print?

```js
class ValidationError extends Error {}
const err = new ValidationError('bad email');
console.log(err.name, String(err));
```

